I found a remaining Windows correctness defect in the third rework: it asks only the leaf/existing-prefix directory whether it is case-sensitive, then uppercases or preserves the entire path. Windows case sensitivity is per directory, so a case-sensitive parent can contain distinct `Foo` and `foo` children even when those child directories themselves are case-insensitive. The current code collapses both complete paths to the same uppercase identity and can redirect lock state to a third spelling. I’m finishing the validation record, then I’ll route this back to implementation with a concrete regression recipe.
